  --title "MACRODEF GEN: ADDR() in macro parameters emitted literally instead of resolved" \
  --label "bug" \
  --body "$(cat <<'EOF'
## Summary

When a MACRODEF is invoked with `ADDR(varname)` as a parameter, the GEN block emits `ADDR ( varname )` literally into the assembly output instead of resolving it to the assembly-level label `_varname`. This produces invalid assembly.

## Reproduction

In `.msw`:
```plsw
MACRODEF CELL_MAKE;
    REQUIRED TAG(expr); REQUIRED PAY(expr); REQUIRED DST(lvalue);
    GEN DO;
        'la r0,{TAG}';
        'lw r0,0(r0)';
        'sll r0,r0,21';
        'la r1,{PAY}';
        'lw r1,0(r1)';
        'or r0,r0,r1';
        'la r1,{DST}';
        'sw r0,0(r1)';
    END;
END;
```

In `.plsw`:
```plsw
DCL G_TAG INT;
DCL G_PAY INT;
DCL G_TMP INT;

G_TAG = 2;
G_PAY = 1;
?CELL_MAKE(TAG(ADDR(G_TAG)), PAY(ADDR(G_PAY)), DST(ADDR(G_TMP)));
```

## Generated assembly (incorrect)

```asm
        la r0,ADDR ( G_TAG )    ; should be: la r0,_G_TAG
        lw r0,0(r0)
        sll r0,r0,21
        la r1,ADDR ( G_PAY )    ; should be: la r1,_G_PAY
        lw r1,0(r1)
        or r0,r0,r1
        la r1,ADDR ( G_TMP )    ; should be: la r1,_G_TMP
        sw r0,0(r1)
```

## Expected

`{TAG}` parameter should resolve `ADDR(G_TAG)` to the assembly label `_G_TAG` before substitution into the GEN block.

## Impact

Blocks all MACRODEF-based cell manipulation in the sw-cor24-prolog LAM VM (CELL_GET_TAG, CELL_GET_PAY, CELL_MAKE, INST_DECODE). Workaround: use arithmetic PROCs instead of macros (with division now fixed by #35).

Found during dogfooding sw-cor24-prolog.
EOF
)"

