# Test: can the compiler handle a PROC with a SELECT that has 7 WHEN clauses?
cat > /tmp/test_select7.plsw <<'EOF'
%DEFINE LIBRARY;
%INCLUDE opcodes;
%INCLUDE vmglob;

TEST: PROC(OP INT) RETURNS(INT);
    SELECT;
        WHEN (OP = 1) DO; RETURN(10); END;
        WHEN (OP = 2) DO; RETURN(20); END;
        WHEN (OP = 3) DO; RETURN(30); END;
        WHEN (OP = 4) DO; RETURN(40); END;
        WHEN (OP = 5) DO; RETURN(50); END;
        WHEN (OP = 6) DO; RETURN(60); END;
        WHEN (OP = 7) DO; RETURN(70); END;
        OTHERWISE DO; RETURN(0); END;
    END;
END;

MAIN: PROC;
END;
EOF

COMPILER_ASM="$HOME/github/sw-embed/sw-cor24-plsw/build/plsw.s"
cor24-run --run "$COMPILER_ASM" -u "$(printf 'c\nFILE:opcodes.msw\n'; cat include/opcodes.msw; printf '\x1E'; printf 'FILE:vmglob.msw\n'; cat include/vmglob.msw; printf '\x1E'; printf 'SOURCE:\n'; cat /tmp/test_select7.plsw; printf '\x04')" -n 500000000 -t 300 --speed 0 2>&1 | sed -n '/^UART output:/,/^Executed /{/^Executed /d;p;}' | sed '1s/^UART output: //' | grep -E "ERROR|failed|assembly" | head -5

gh issue create -R sw-embed/sw-cor24-plsw \
  --title "Compiler crashes on deeply nested IF/ELSE inside SELECT/WHEN" \
  --label "bug" \
  --body "$(cat <<'BODY'
## Summary

The PL/SW compiler crashes (re-enters _start) when compiling a PROC with nested IF/ELSE/DO blocks inside a SELECT/WHEN clause. This may be related to #33 (IF/ELSE chain limit).

## Reproduction

The following compiles and crashes:
```plsw
%DEFINE LIBRARY;
%INCLUDE vmglob;

EXEC_DATA: PROC(PC INT) RETURNS(INT);
    DCL IMM INT;
    DCL REGVAL INT;
    SELECT;
        WHEN (G_OP = 18) DO;
            IMM = MEM(PC + 1);
            REGVAL = 0;
            IF (REGVAL = 1) THEN DO;
                MEM(PC) = IMM;
            END;
            ELSE DO;
                IF (REGVAL = IMM) THEN DO;
                    MEM(PC) = 0;
                END;
                ELSE DO;
                    IF (G_OP = 0) THEN DO;
                        G_RUNNING = 0;
                    END;
                    ELSE DO;
                        MEM(PC) = 1;
                    END;
                END;
            END;
        END;
        OTHERWISE DO;
            RETURN(0);
        END;
    END;
    RETURN(1);
END;

MAIN: PROC;
END;
```

The compiler outputs "--- compiling ---" then crashes (reprints the banner, indicating _start re-entry).

A simpler SELECT with 7 WHEN clauses (no deep nesting) compiles fine. The issue is specifically the 3-level deep IF/ELSE/DO nesting inside a WHEN block.

## Impact

Blocks compilation of opcode handler modules in sw-cor24-prolog where GET_CONST has: deref -> if unbound then bind else if match then ok else if choice-point then backtrack else fail.

Found during dogfooding sw-cor24-prolog.
BODY
)"

