gh issue comment 39 -R sw-embed/sw-cor24-plsw --body "$(cat <<'BODY'
Additional finding: **nested SELECT inside SELECT** also crashes the compiler, not just nested IF/ELSE.

Example from vm_builtin.plsw — a SELECT/WHEN that contains an inner SELECT:
```plsw
EXEC_BUILTIN: PROC(PC INT) RETURNS(INT);
    SELECT;
        WHEN (G_OP = OP_B_WRITE) DO;
            /* ... */
            SELECT;                  /* <-- inner SELECT crashes */
                WHEN (WTAG = 2) DO; /* ... */ END;
                WHEN (WTAG = 1) DO; /* ... */ END;
                OTHERWISE DO; /* ... */ END;
            END;
        END;
        /* more WHENs ... */
    END;
END;
```

This blocks splitting the VM dispatch into handler modules since the B_WRITE opcode needs inner dispatch on cell tag type.

Workaround: extract inner SELECT into a separate PROC.
BODY
