gh issue create -R sw-embed/sw-cor24-plsw \
  --title "Compiler crash/timeout with 70+ %DEFINE macros across multiple .msw includes" \
  --label "bug" \
  --body "$(cat <<'BODY'
## Summary

The compiler crashes or runs indefinitely when a .plsw file includes multiple .msw headers that together define 70+ %DEFINE macros. Individually each include compiles fine.

## Reproduction

```bash
# Works: 2 includes, ~32 defines
cat > /tmp/test.plsw <<'EOF'
%DEFINE LIBRARY;
%INCLUDE opcodes;
%INCLUDE vmglob;
HELLO: PROC; CALL UART_PUTCHAR(72); END;
MAIN: PROC; END;
EOF
# pipeline.sh include/opcodes.msw include/vmglob.msw /tmp/test.plsw
# Result: OK (32M cycles)

# Fails: 3 includes, ~74 defines
cat > /tmp/test.plsw <<'EOF'
%DEFINE LIBRARY;
%INCLUDE memory;
%INCLUDE opcodes;
%INCLUDE vmglob;
HELLO: PROC; CALL UART_PUTCHAR(72); END;
MAIN: PROC; END;
EOF
# pipeline.sh include/memory.msw include/opcodes.msw include/vmglob.msw /tmp/test.plsw
# Result: 1B+ cycles, compiler crashes (reprints banner)
```

Define counts: memory.msw has 42 %DEFINE, opcodes.msw has 32 %DEFINE = 74 total.

## Context

- #16 raised DEF_MAX from 32 to some higher value
- The current DEF_MAX may still be too low, or the macro expansion loop becomes pathologically slow with many defines
- This blocks compilation of any VM module that needs both memory and opcode constants (5 of 9 modules)

Found during dogfooding sw-cor24-prolog.
BODY
)"

