gh issue create -R sw-embed/sw-cor24-plsw \
  --title "PROC-local DCL STATIC INIT: data label not emitted in assembly" \
  --label "bug" \
  --body "$(cat <<'BODY'
## Summary

When a PROC declares a local variable with STATIC INIT, the compiler accepts the syntax and generates a reference (`la r0,_VARNAME`) but never emits the corresponding data label and initialized bytes.

## Reproduction

```plsw
%DEFINE LIBRARY;
TEST: PROC;
    DCL MSG(6) CHAR STATIC INIT('hello');
    CALL UART_PUTS(ADDR(MSG));
END;
MAIN: PROC; END;
```

Generated assembly:
```asm
; DCL MSG(6) CHAR STATIC INIT('hello');
; CALL UART_PUTS(ADDR(MSG));
        la      r0,_MSG        ; reference to _MSG
```

Missing: `_MSG:` label with `.byte 104,101,108,108,111,0` data.

## Expected

The compiler should emit the static data section for PROC-local STATIC INIT variables, with a label that the reference can resolve to.

## Context

PL/SW usage.md (lines 369-387) recommends PROC-local STATIC for module-private persistent state in library modules. This pattern is needed because top-level DCLs are suppressed in LIBRARY mode.

Found during modular build of sw-cor24-prolog LAM VM.
BODY
)"

gh issue create -R sw-embed/sw-cor24-plsw \
  --title "PROC-local STATIC DCLs exported as global labels, causing link24 duplicates" \
  --label "bug" \
  --body "$(cat <<'BODY'
## Summary

PROC-local STATIC DCLs emit their data with global labels (e.g., `_M_FAIL:`) instead of module-private/local labels. When multiple library modules each declare `DCL M_FAIL(7) CHAR STATIC INIT(...)` inside different PROCs, link24 sees duplicate `_M_FAIL` exports and fails.

## Reproduction

Two library modules each with a PROC-local STATIC:

```plsw
/* vm_data.plsw */
%DEFINE LIBRARY;
%INCLUDE vmglob;
VM_BACKTRACK: PROC;
    DCL M_FAIL(7) CHAR STATIC INIT('FAIL  ');
    CALL UART_PUTS(ADDR(M_FAIL));
END;
MAIN: PROC; END;
```

```plsw
/* vm_ctrl.plsw */
%DEFINE LIBRARY;
%INCLUDE vmglob;
EXEC_CTRL: PROC(PC INT) RETURNS(INT);
    DCL M_FAIL(7) CHAR STATIC INIT('FAIL  ');
    CALL UART_PUTS(ADDR(M_FAIL));
    RETURN(1);
END;
MAIN: PROC; END;
```

Both compile to assembly containing `.globl _M_FAIL` / `_M_FAIL:`. meta-gen prep puts `DEF _M_FAIL` in both .syms files. link24 fails:

```
link24: error: duplicate export '_M_FAIL' in module 'vm_data' (already defined)
```

## Expected

PROC-local STATIC data should use a module-private or mangled label (e.g., `_vm_data__M_FAIL` or a local label like `L42`) so it doesn't conflict across modules. PROC-local STATIC variables are module-internal by definition — they should not appear as exported symbols.

## Context

This is the recommended pattern from usage.md (lines 369-387) for module-private persistent state in LIBRARY modules. Without it, library modules have no way to own string constants.

Found during modular build of sw-cor24-prolog (9 modules, link24 step).
BODY
)"

